# The same policy as ../input.lg with the gates declared in reverse order
# (D, E, C, B, A). Verdicts and decision are unchanged (SPEC §7.5, rule 2).
# The §7.4 tie-break: A is the only gate with no unlogged activated
# predecessor, so it is logged first although declared last; then B, C and E
# are all eligible and E is declared earliest, then C, then B; D last. The
# log runs A, E, C, B, D (rule 3).
actor a
gate  D grant a
gate  E grant a
gate  C
gate  B grant a
gate  A grant a
cord a -> A
cord A -> B
cord A -> C
cord A -> E
cord B -> D
cord C -> D
cord E -> D
cord D -> master
